      "side": 1,
      "message": "`PCIE_QCOM` can only be built-in, and this option selects tristate `PCI_PWRCTRL_SLOT` because of dependencies. So we\u0027ve had these two built-in for a while. No change there.\n\nThe difference in v7.0 is that commit https://git.kernel.org/torvalds/c/9cb64f61ec7a now adds select from `PCI_PWRCTRL_SLOT` to `POWER_SEQUENCING`. This forces the module `pwrseq-core.ko` to be built-in instead. Only that.\n\nThis is an upstream dependency. If we want to support modular dependency and switch the `select` to `imply` I think QCOM would need to work on managing the dependency at runtime (if possible). It should be doable. I\u0027ll open a conversation with them.",
